---
description: Track and disconnect GNOME Shell signal handlers in disable(). Use when connecting to Main.panel, Main.overview, settings, or any object this feature does not destroy.
alwaysApply: false
---

# Signals

Track every `connect()` on an object this feature does not own, and disconnect those ids in `disable()`. Put this helper in `lib/signals.js` when a feature first needs it.

```javascript
import GObject from 'gi://GObject';

export class SignalTracker {
    constructor() {
        this._connections = [];
    }

    connect(object, signal, callback) {
        const id = object.connect(signal, callback);
        this._connections.push({object, id});
        return id;
    }

    disconnectAll() {
        while (this._connections.length > 0) {
            const {object, id} = this._connections.pop();

            try {
                if (id && GObject.signal_handler_is_connected(object, id))
                    object.disconnect(id);
            } catch (e) {
                // The object may already be gone during session shutdown.
            }
        }
    }
}
```

```javascript
// ❌ BAD
Main.panel.connect('scroll-event', (_actor, event) => this._onScroll(event));

// ✅ GOOD
this._signals.connect(Main.panel, 'scroll-event', (_actor, event) => {
    this._onScroll(event);
});
```

`connectObject(signal, callback, owner)` is only for an actor this feature creates and destroys. Shell objects this feature does not destroy go through `SignalTracker`, including settings changes.
